From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:30:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] background: One add button, the animation as a group of its
 own
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plinius: each section of the Background page had a row of its own to add
files (Add Video…, Add 360° Photo…, Add Picture…). There is one button in
the page's header bar instead (+, "Add Pictures and Videos"): the file
dialog offers pictures, and videos and GIFs with plinius-ambient 0.5, and
each file goes into its section by its type: videos and GIFs to Video,
equirectangular photos (GPano XMP) to 360° Photos, other pictures to Own
Pictures. The sections that got something open. A section without
anything shows "Nothing added yet".

The animated effect and its amount are no section among the background's
any more but the group "Animation" on top of the page (Effect, Amount):
they are drawn over whatever the background is.

The rows Style and Background on the Appearance page have nothing in front
any more (no accent dot, no small picture); their subtitles say what is
set. The panel no longer makes a thumbnail for the row.

The sorting and copying are in cc-plinius-panorama.c, the group in
cc-plinius-ambient.c, the rows in cc-plinius-appearance.c (our own files).
